# Player Activity Assumptions

Define and document a reasonable typical-player model before tuning the progression.

Unless the existing game provides better usage data, simulate a typical player who:

* Logs in at least once per day.
* Uses approximately 75–85% of generated exploration energy.
* Performs regular defense sessions.
* Does not use paid progression boosts.
* Purchases equipment at reasonable intervals rather than saving all gold indefinitely.
* Uses an average-quality stat allocation.
* Attempts newly unlocked dungeon levels but sometimes returns to easier levels for gold or equipment.
* Experiences some unsuccessful encounters and defense runs.

Also simulate:

* A casual player using approximately 40–50% of available actions.
* A dedicated player using approximately 95–100% of available actions.

The dedicated player may progress faster, but the game must not allow dungeon level 20 to be reached in only a few months.

