# Exploration Energy

Exploration energy currently regenerates at the following rate:

* One energy every 120 minutes.
* Each explore level reduces the regeneration time by one minute.
* Regeneration time has a minimum of 30 minutes.

The player should reach the 30-minute minimum after approximately one year of typical daily play.

This means the explore-level XP curve must be balanced so the player gains the required number of explore levels over approximately 365 days.

Clarify whether the existing project treats the starting explore level as level 0 or level 1, and account for the resulting one-level difference.

After the 30-minute minimum has been reached:

* Explore levels must continue increasing.
* Energy regeneration must remain at 30 minutes.
* Additional explore levels should primarily increase exploration gold.
* Post-cap gold growth must be gradual and controlled.
* Post-cap levels may provide very small secondary benefits only when they improve the game without causing runaway scaling.

Store the following as configurable values rather than scattering them through the code:

* Starting energy regeneration time.
* Minimum regeneration time.
* Reduction per explore level.
* Explore level at which the minimum is reached.
* Post-cap gold multiplier growth.
* XP curve constants.

Use timestamps to calculate regeneration. Do not depend on a continuously running timer.

