# Passive Defense Combat

Combat occurs passively while the player is defending.

## Defense Session Rules

* The player starts a defense session through the existing interface or command.
* The initial maximum defense duration is one hour.
* The game stores the defense start timestamp.
* Combat is not calculated continuously.
* Combat is resolved when the player next performs an action that ends defense, including:

  * Exploring.
  * Manually stopping defense.
  * Starting another incompatible activity.
* Only completed minutes count.
* One enemy encounter occurs for each completed defense minute.
* A loss immediately ends the defense run.
* No encounters after the first loss grant rewards.
* Player HP carries from one battle to the next during the session.
* Clearly define whether HP is restored when a new defense session begins. Unless the existing design specifies otherwise, begin each new defense session at full HP.
* The same defense session must never be claimable twice.

Add protection against:

* Repeatedly claiming the same elapsed time.
* Negative elapsed time.
* Device clock changes where practical.
* Invalid or corrupted defense timestamps.
* Starting multiple simultaneous defense sessions.
* Integer overflow during long offline periods.

