# Required Acceptance Tests

The completed implementation must demonstrate that:

1. Energy begins at one point every 120 minutes.
2. Energy regeneration cannot become faster than one point every 30 minutes.
3. Explore levels continue after the regeneration cap.
4. Post-cap explore levels increase gold without reducing regeneration further.
5. A defense session begins with the correct duration.
6. Defense elapsed time is calculated from timestamps.
7. Each completed defense minute produces no more than one enemy encounter.
8. A player loss ends the defense run immediately.
9. HP carries between battles in the same session.
10. The same defense session cannot be claimed twice.
11. Combat level increases maximum defense duration correctly.
12. Defense duration never exceeds eight hours.
13. Multiple combat levels grant all HP and stat-point rewards.
14. Damage cannot become negative.
15. Battles cannot become infinite.
16. Equipment is available throughout levels 1–400.
17. Normal sub-300 equipment availability ranges are approximately 10–20 levels.
18. High-level equipment may use wider ranges.
19. Higher shop levels have improved rarity probabilities.
20. The shop never produces an empty slot because of invalid rarity filtering.
21. Every dungeon level has valid exploration and combat content.
22. Dungeon 18 and dungeon 20 progression approximates the requested timelines.
23. Existing saves migrate without losing legitimate progress.
24. All edited JSON files pass parsing and schema validation.

